# Family A22: asynchronous publish completion (internal/completion).
# See hack/bakeoff.sh.
PKG=./internal/completion
BENCH=BenchmarkPublish/Async
REF=inline
AUTO_KEY=completion
ADR=17
TITLE="Async completion (A22)"
# §9 A22 asks for a zero-allocation callback default: the adapters allocate
# their handle per message (future 2, channel 3) and have to earn it.
# BenchmarkPublishAwait is the adapter-only cost and is reported, not scored.

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="0-alloc callback default; inline only if documented and never under locks"
# MATRIX=default: the criterion is allocations per message, which every
# in-flight window reports identically, and the default grid brackets the
# window at 1 and 64. `full` adds 8 and 512 -- more of the same curve for
# twelve more rows -- and reads nothing the criterion asks for (assumption
# A24.61).
MATRIX=default
DECIDED_AT="inflight=1 inflight=64"
DECIDED_ON="allocs/op ns/op"
# This family had NO benchmark common to its four kinds, so `bakeoff decide`
# would have failed with "no benchmark is present for every kind" after paying
# for the whole measurement. The cause was the naming, not the kinds: `inline`
# and `deferred` produced `Async/<kind>/inflight=N` while `future` and
# `channel` produced `Async/<kind>/<base>/inflight=N`, because those two are
# adapters over a base rather than peers of it. The family's shape is two
# delivery positions crossed with the three things a caller can be handed, and
# the four Kinds are the four values `Auto` can resolve to: the adapters' base
# arm is now named `Async/<kind>/inflight=N` like the callback kinds' -- the
# kind in its own delivery position, which is the row the four are compared on
# -- and their second arm stays `Async/<kind>/deferred/inflight=N`, which is
# the crossing §10.5's {inline,deferred} names and the evidence for "inline
# only if documented". Assumption A24.63.
